## 👥 Team Members (`OurTeam`) Payload & User Link Integration

`OurTeam` endpoints (`/our-teams/`) support optional linking to a registered `UserAccount` or fallback to direct `name` & `phone_number` fields.

* **Payload Fields:**
  * `user_id`: (Integer, optional) Primary key of the `UserAccount`.
  * `name`: (String, optional if `user_id` is provided) Member's full name.
  * `phone_number`: (String, optional) Phone number.
  * `position`: (String, required) Job title / position in company.
  * `bio`: (HTML/Text, optional) Extended bio / statement.
  * `image_media_id`: (MediaAsset ID, optional) Member photo.
  * `facebook_url`: (URL string, optional) Facebook profile link.
  * `instagram_url`: (URL string, optional) Instagram profile link.
  * `twitter_url`: (URL string, optional) Twitter/X profile link.
  * `linkedin_url`: (URL string, optional) LinkedIn profile link.
  * `github_url`: (URL string, optional) GitHub profile link.

* **Response Helper Properties:**
  * `display_name`: Automatically returns `user.first_name + user.last_name` / `user.email` if linked to `user`, otherwise returns `name`.
  * `display_phone_number`: Automatically returns `user.phone_number` if present, otherwise returns `phone_number`.
  * `user_details`: Object containing `{ id, email, first_name, last_name }` if linked to a user.

---

## 🖼 Relational & Media Asset Handling

When creating or updating entities with media library foreign keys (`logo_media_id`, `image_media_id`, `hero_image_media_id`, `pic_media_id`):

1. **Assigning Media Asset:**
   Frontends can pass an integer ID, string ID, or nested object:
   ```json
   {
     "title": "Cloud Migration",
     "description": "Enterprise cloud services",
     "image_media_id": 14
   }
   ```
   Or nested object:
   ```json
   {
     "title": "Cloud Migration",
     "description": "Enterprise cloud services",
     "image_media": { "id": 14 }
   }
   ```
2. **Clearing Media Asset:**
   To remove an existing media association, pass `null`:
   ```json
   {
     "image_media_id": null
   }
   ```

---

## 🏷 Many-to-Many Category Resolution

For entities supporting categories (`Service`, `Product`):
* Pass an array of category IDs under `category_ids` or `category`:
  ```json
  {
    "title": "Web App Development",
    "description": "Custom DRF & React apps",
    "category_ids": [1, 3]
  }
  ```

---

## 🔀 Automatic Unique Slug Generation

* Models with slugs (`Service`, `Product`, `Event`) accept an optional custom `slug` string in payload data.
* If `slug` is omitted or left empty, the backend `pre_save` signal automatically generates a URL-safe, unique slug based on `title` or `name` (appending a suffix if a collision occurs).

---

## 💻 Frontend Code Examples (TypeScript / Axios)

### 1. Fetch List of Services
```typescript
import axios from 'axios';

export interface Service {
  id: number;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  image_url: string;
  slug: string;
  image_media?: {
    id: number;
    url: string;
  };
}

export const fetchServices = async (): Promise<Service[]> => {
  const response = await axios.get<Service[]>('https://your-api.com/api/our-services/');
  return response.data;
};
```

### 2. Fetch Single Service by Slug
```typescript
export const fetchServiceBySlug = async (slug: string): Promise<Service> => {
  const response = await axios.get<Service>(`https://your-api.com/api/our-services/${slug}/`);
  return response.data;
};
```

### 3. Create New Team Member Linked to UserAccount
```typescript
export const createTeamMember = async (data: {
  user_id?: number;
  name?: string;
  phone_number?: string;
  position: string;
  bio?: string;
  image_media_id?: number;
  facebook_url?: string;
  instagram_url?: string;
  twitter_url?: string;
  linkedin_url?: string;
  github_url?: string;
}, token: string) => {
  const response = await axios.post(
    'https://your-api.com/api/our-teams/',
    data,
    {
      headers: {
        Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      },
    }
  );
  return response.data;
};
```

### 4. Update Company Info (Singleton)
```typescript
export const updateCompanyInfo = async (data: {
  company_name?: string;
  email?: string;
  telephone?: string;
  logo_media_id?: number | null;
}, token: string) => {
  const response = await axios.patch(
    'https://your-api.com/api/company-info/',
    data,
    {
      headers: {
        Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      },
    }
  );
  return response.data;
};
```

### 5. Public Contact Form Submission
```typescript
export const submitContactForm = async (formData: {
  full_name: string;
  email: string;
  phone_number?: string;
  message: string;
}) => {
  const response = await axios.post(
    'https://your-api.com/api/contact-us/',
    formData
  );
  return response.data;
};
```
